\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {IV}{\ignorespaces The simulations: the drainhole family (a), in code units. Model D$n$ is the drainhole background with $v_e\approx n/100$ (D0: static). $8\pi J/A$ is the angular momentum as a percentage of its extremal value $J_{\rm  ext}=A/8\pi $ at the throat area $A$, and $M_{\rm  ADM}$ the mass of the $\eta \to +\infty $ end (both from the background tables). The finest $\Delta x$ is $0.0625$ at $N=128$ on $L=64$ and at $N=256$ on $L=128$, and scales inversely with $N$ within a triplet. $\sigma $ is the Kreiss--Oliger dissipation strength (Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:scheme}); the conformal factor is floored at $10^{-8}$, except at $10^{-4}$ in the D90 runs. Damping: the boundary damping layer of Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:boundary} on, or the background-relative boundary alone (off). Conv.\ $t$: the time up to which the results are converged and quoted. $\tau $: the $e$-fold time of the unstable mode (Sec.~\ref {sec:slow}); MOTS: the marginally outer-trapped surface (Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:runs}). GW: the $(2,0)$ burst at $R=14$ arrives within the converged span (burst), is still rising at its end (onset), or stays below the extraction floor (none). The D59 and D70 runs are still in progress.}}{6}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:ladder}{{IV}{6}{The simulations: the drainhole family (a), in code units. Model D$n$ is the drainhole background with $v_e\approx n/100$ (D0: static). $8\pi J/A$ is the angular momentum as a percentage of its extremal value $J_{\rm ext}=A/8\pi $ at the throat area $A$, and $M_{\rm ADM}$ the mass of the $\eta \to +\infty $ end (both from the background tables). The finest $\Delta x$ is $0.0625$ at $N=128$ on $L=64$ and at $N=256$ on $L=128$, and scales inversely with $N$ within a triplet. $\sigma $ is the Kreiss--Oliger dissipation strength (Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:scheme}); the conformal factor is floored at $10^{-8}$, except at $10^{-4}$ in the D90 runs. Damping: the boundary damping layer of Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:boundary} on, or the background-relative boundary alone (off). Conv.\ $t$: the time up to which the results are converged and quoted. $\tau $: the $e$-fold time of the unstable mode (Sec.~\ref {sec:slow}); MOTS: the marginally outer-trapped surface (Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:runs}). GW: the $(2,0)$ burst at $R=14$ arrives within the converged span (burst), is still rising at its end (onset), or stays below the extraction floor (none). The D59 and D70 runs are still in progress}{table.4}{}}
