\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The inverse $e$-fold time $1/\tau $ of the throat's areal radius (left axis; $\tau $ on the right) against the angular momentum as a fraction of its extremal value. Filled circles: collapsing models; filled triangles: expanding models; open circle: D90, no growth to $t=150$; every $\tau $ is the offset-free fit of Sec.~\ref {sec:slow} and a row of Table~\ref {tab:ladder}. Dashed: the fit $a-b\,(J/A)^2$ through the collapse branch alone, zero at $32\%$. Open diamonds: the second-order rates of Refs.~\cite  {azad2023,azad2024} at $C=1$; dotted rules: their conjectured end of the instability (${\approx }30\%$) and the zero of their second-order rate ($33\%$). Past the crossing the unperturbed throat expands with a rate that rises with spin.}}{7}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:curve}{{4}{7}{The inverse $e$-fold time $1/\tau $ of the throat's areal radius (left axis; $\tau $ on the right) against the angular momentum as a fraction of its extremal value. Filled circles: collapsing models; filled triangles: expanding models; open circle: D90, no growth to $t=150$; every $\tau $ is the offset-free fit of Sec.~\ref {sec:slow} and a row of Table~\ref {tab:ladder}. Dashed: the fit $a-b\,(J/A)^2$ through the collapse branch alone, zero at $32\%$. Open diamonds: the second-order rates of Refs.~\cite {azad2023,azad2024} at $C=1$; dotted rules: their conjectured end of the instability (${\approx }30\%$) and the zero of their second-order rate ($33\%$). Past the crossing the unperturbed throat expands with a rate that rises with spin}{figure.4}{}}
