\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Stability of the D90 model over its triplet $N=128/192/256$ ($L=128$; finest $\Delta x$ in each panel title), to $t=150$. (a)--(h)~Constraint norms per level with the same second-/fourth-order brackets as Fig.~\ref {fig:conv02}: every level converges with resolution over the run. (i)~The equatorial throat radius holds the stationary value, its offset falling with resolution. (j)~The areal throat radius drifts by $\le 7\times 10^{-5}$ over the full run. (k)~The $(2,0)$ extraction at $R=18$, relative to its $t=0$ read-off: fluctuations at the $10^{-4}$ level, no burst. (l)~The lapse at the $\eta \to -\infty $ puncture falls smoothly at all three resolutions (the gauge, not the geometry). The D90 throat shows no growing radius and no wave at any resolution over the run, with constraint norms converging.}}{11}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:conv09}{{7}{11}{Stability of the D90 model over its triplet $N=128/192/256$ ($L=128$; finest $\Delta x$ in each panel title), to $t=150$. (a)--(h)~Constraint norms per level with the same second-/fourth-order brackets as Fig.~\ref {fig:conv02}: every level converges with resolution over the run. (i)~The equatorial throat radius holds the stationary value, its offset falling with resolution. (j)~The areal throat radius drifts by $\le 7\times 10^{-5}$ over the full run. (k)~The $(2,0)$ extraction at $R=18$, relative to its $t=0$ read-off: fluctuations at the $10^{-4}$ level, no burst. (l)~The lapse at the $\eta \to -\infty $ puncture falls smoothly at all three resolutions (the gauge, not the geometry). The D90 throat shows no growing radius and no wave at any resolution over the run, with constraint norms converging}{figure.7}{}}
